From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 06 Nov 2026 18:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] user32: the message box as the approved prototype draws it.

The message box was Wine's classic one: text and buttons centred, a 16 px icon at the left, no footer, and the
controls drawn as the classic ones, which the prototype (prototypes/windows11-shell js/dialogs.js D.messageBox,
css/dialogs.css .dlg-msg) does not. On the shell's scorecard the four message box states (msgbox, msgbox-error,
msgbox-info, taskdialog) stood at 2% to 12% of their pixels within one level of the prototype's.

- dlls/user32/msgbox.c: the prototype's layout. The body's margins are its 26 px above and below, 24 px left and
  30 px right; the dialog icon is its 32 px pixels over a 42 px column (MB_USERICON's own stays the static control);
  the text is 12 px on 16 px lines, measured as the prototype measures it (its longest line unwrapped, never past
  5/8 of the work area less the body's margins, then wrapped there); the dialog's size is the prototype's formula
  (the text plus 54 px and the icon's column, at least the footer's buttons, at least the caption's needs, never
  under 180 px), centred on the work area as before. The footer is its 49 px strip with the buttons right-aligned,
  26 px tall, 88 px wide at least, 10 px apart and 12 px in from the sides; their style is BS_OWNERDRAW and
  WM_DRAWITEM paints the prototype's four button looks. The body is its white page and the footer its #f3f3f3
  strip; the dialog keeps the light palette in the dark theme, as the prototype's classic dialogs do.
- The pixels: pw_dialog_sprites.h, the prototype's warning, error, info and question icons and its button looks
  measured by tools/build-dialog-sprites.py from themes/windows11/dialogs/*.json (already in the tree).
- Not gated yet; the message box states' scores are in docs/SHELL81_REVIEW.md once a build of this tree has run.

The prototype's dialogs keep their light palette; this patch does not yet make the dark theme's *caption* of a
message box light (the prototype's is), so the dark states' caption bars still follow the app's theme.
--- a/dlls/user32/msgbox.c
+++ b/dlls/user32/msgbox.c
@@ -34,6 +34,91 @@
